course: dictionary
lesson: 6495
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and neat is one of them. The dictionary gives five, so you cannot pick one just from the word itself. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Keep your room neat» means keep it tidy and in good order. But «neat handwriting» is about how clearly and carefully the letters are made. Same word, different job.
explain: «That's a neat trick!» is informal, and it means very good or cool. It has nothing to do with being tidy. Look at what is being described: a trick is something you watch, not a room you keep.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «In his neat little house» works with tidy: a tidy little house. «A neat solution» works with clever and simple. If your meaning does not fit, try another one from the dictionary.
fact: Neat has several meanings, so always check the sentence around it.
fact: «Neat» can mean tidy and in good order, as in «a neat bedroom».
fact: «Neat» can mean done carefully and clearly, as in «neat handwriting».
fact: «Neat» can mean clever and simple, as in «a neat solution», and informally it can mean very good or cool, as in «That's a neat trick!».
fact: A neat drink is one with no water or ice added.
exercise: «In his neat little house she finds the fan and gloves, but also a bottle with no label.» What does neat mean here? | Very old and falling down | Noisy and busy | *Tidy and in good order | Covered in mud
exercise: «A mirror reflects light in a neat way, so it shows a clear image.» What does neat suggest here? | Messy and scattered | Very loud | Hidden under a cloth | *Clear and precise
exercise: «Cartoonists often draw four fingers because it is quicker and looks neater.» Why does the author use neater? | *Simpler and tidier to look at | It takes longer to draw | It has more fingers | More realistic, like a real hand
test: Ella says, «That's neat!» about a magic trick. What does she mean? | Tidy and in order | Quiet and calm | Made with water | *Very good, cool
test: «Her neat handwriting made her answers easy to check.» What does neat mean here? | Very loud and bold | Very old and worn | Made from ice | *Done carefully and clearly
exam: «Some girls sneer ‘Princess Lily’ because her hair is neat and her books are tidy.» Which word best matches neat here? | *Tidy | Ancient | Barely | Noisy
